{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that strict order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the minimum spanning forest is unique, and this is it, whichever algorithm runs: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canonical forest, listed in nondecreasing weight and, among equal weights, in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, with the weight added up in that order. Currently Kruskal’s algorithm on sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) and otherwise Prim’s under that order followed by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sort of the n − 1 edges taken, which is faster on denser graphs (see the benchmarks)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop, never for a self-loop, and not kept."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights, and so are infinities. A NaN weight traps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX instead offers "},{"code":"ignore_nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; filter such edges out first)."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not overflow and is not NaN."}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and igraph’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum_spanning_tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpanningTrees"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Kruskal.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L24"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documen